35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission trial worked, but the shared nursing round failed due to logistics.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The booking system misses unlogged work, and our rooms and parking are already full.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The joint clinic failed because neither department owned the budget. Data agreements take too long.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Ward vacancies are high, and agency costs are rising. Midwifery has slack, though.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The budget is down a quarter, and off-site visits earn no tariff. We must be careful.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if off-site visits earn nothing, how do we justify a home follow-up team?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, that is a valid point. The financial model for home visits is weak.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the midwifery slack is interesting. Could we leverage that for a new service?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, yes, but we must ensure it doesn't strain the already thin ward nursing.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, the full rooms suggest we need a program that doesn't require new physical space.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission data shows home visits work, but the funding model is the problem.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"A day rehabilitation unit would need dedicated space, which we lack.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Chronic care coordination could work if we avoid the joint ownership trap.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"Perinatal support could use the midwifery slack, but we need to check the pediatric side.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,We need a program that fits within the reduced budget and existing infrastructure.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I am leaning towards a program that leverages existing staff without new rooms.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,Agreed. We must avoid anything that requires new construction or major IT changes.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am concerned about the long-term sustainability of any new arrangement.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I want to make sure the staffing burden is fair and manageable.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,Let us consider the candidates with these constraints in mind.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
